# The host's path to the guest delays 1.5 s, then 50 ms from 5 s on: every sample after the drop
# lies far ahead of the guest's clock line. The first is dropped as a lone outlier; 8 that agree
# restart the clock on them, and the copies catch up by a jump the render offset absorbs.
# Bounds, derived: the worlds agree at rest (the copy caught up); behind_ticks.max is delay_max
# (15) plus the 1.5 s one way (90 ticks) plus 2 for the arrival and read ticks: 107.
scenario latency_drop
scene two_chars_item
seed 7
guests 1
settle 4s

net g1 to_guest delay 1500ms
at 5s net g1 to_guest delay 50ms

at 7s p0 walk 2 1 as a
p0 walk -2 0 as b
p0 walk 2 -1 as c

expect result c done
expect agree_at_rest 5cm
expect behind_ticks.max <= 107t
